WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.620
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 4, Network security, which is 14 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.293
This lesson covers objective 4 point 1.

00:00:10.293 --> 00:00:14.269
Explain the importance of basic network security concepts.

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:20.300
Today's concept: the transport and port for TACACS plus, and how it differs from RADIUS.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:25.688
A network device sends logins to an AAA server.

00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:28.680
Two common choices are TACACS plus and RADIUS.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.630
TACACS plus travels over TCP, port forty nine.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.512
RADIUS travels over UDP.

00:00:34.512 --> 00:00:40.360
Port eighteen twelve carries authentication, and port eighteen thirteen carries accounting.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.709
The common mix-up is to pair TACACS plus with UDP eighteen twelve.

00:00:44.709 --> 00:00:46.410
That port belongs to RADIUS.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.958
A simple hook: T for TCP, T for TACACS plus.

00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:56.190
TACACS plus also protects the whole packet body, while RADIUS hides only the password.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.238
For the exam, TACACS plus is T for TCP, port forty nine.

00:01:02.238 --> 00:01:08.331
RADIUS is UDP, with eighteen twelve for authentication and eighteen thirteen for accounting.

00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:10.450
That's objective four point one.
